\p \v 20 \w On that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, \w HOLY|strong="H6944"\w* \w TO THE LORD|strong="H3068"\w*\f + \fr 14:20 \ft That is, \fqa the LORD\f* \w will be [inscribed]|strong="H1961"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the bells|strong="H4698"\w* \w of the horses|strong="H5483"\w*, \w and the cooking pots|strong="H5518"\w* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w like the sprinkling bowls|strong="H4219"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the altar|strong="H4196"\w*. \v 21 \w Indeed, every|strong="H3605"\w* \w pot|strong="H5518"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w and Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w holy|strong="H6944"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w who sacrifice|strong="H2076"\w* \w will come|strong="H935"\w* \w and take|strong="H3947"\w* some [pots] \w and cook|strong="H1310"\w* in them. \w And on that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w there will no|strong="H3808"\w* \w longer|strong="H5750"\w* \w be|strong="H1961"\w* \w a Canaanite|strong="H3669"\w*\f + \fr 14:21 \ft Or \fqa merchant\f* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w*.
